The Linux 2.4.70 kernel has been released a few days ago, it contains =
lots of changes means, according to Linux, a milestone in its way to 2.6 =
release. Andrew Morton and other kernel devs are working hard, and 2.5 =
kernel series are starting a stablizing process, so we can expect a 2.6 =
release in about 4 or 5 months if the developement goes on that fast. =
But how about Reiser4 ?
Hans said it would be available as 2.6 kernel comes out, but do you =
really think you'll be able to achieve the last part of the developement =
until 2.6 ?
Would Linus integrate Reiser4 in the 2.6 kernel even if the testing =
process is not complete (he personally said 2.6 kernel will still need =
lots of testing even after its release) ?
Do you plan to link Reiser4 release with the 2.6 kernel announcement ?
How about the BitKeeper repositery : does it contain the latest 2.5 =
kernel sources along with your Reiser4 developement patches ?

